index 00000000..f5d939ef
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.claude/agent-memory/asd-dev/feedback_hosted-service-ctor-options.md
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+---
+name: hosted-service-ctor-options
+description: Singleton hosted services must not read validated IOptions in their constructor chain, or the build-time OpenAPI generation fails.
+metadata:
+  type: feedback
+---
+
+A `BackgroundService` registered with `AddHostedService` is constructed whenever the host is built, including by the OpenAPI document generation that runs inside `dotnet build` of `Competency.Api`; there `App:PublicBaseUrl` and similar validated options are unset, so any dependency that reads `IOptions<T>.Value` in its constructor (for example `PromotionCalendar`) throws `OptionsValidationException` and fails the build.
+
+**Why:** the failure surfaces as 40 cryptic `Microsoft.Extensions.ApiDescription.Server` errors, not as a compile error.
+
+**How to apply:** give a hosted service only dependencies that are cheap to build (`IServiceScopeFactory`, `TimeProvider`, logger, the mail queue); resolve option-reading services from a per-pass scope inside the loop.
diff --git a/.claude/agent-memory/asd-dev/feedback_windows-scripted-edits.md b/.claude/agent-memory/asd-dev/feedback_windows-scripted-edits.md
index b791480e..a7bcbe22 100644
--- a/.claude/agent-memory/asd-dev/feedback_windows-scripted-edits.md
+++ b/.claude/agent-memory/asd-dev/feedback_windows-scripted-edits.md
@@ -15,4 +15,8 @@ Creating a large new `.tsx` file through a Bash `cat <<'EOF'` heredoc once faile
 
 The working tree is mixed: `git ls-files --eol` shows many `.cs` files `w/crlf` and others `w/lf` (index is LF for all). A multi-line anchor from a script never matches a CRLF file; read the file, normalise to `\n` for matching, and write back with the file's own EOL (a small `Doc` helper in the scratchpad). A script whose `str.replace` silently no-ops leaves the file unmodified — check `git status` after.
 
+A Python edit opened without `encoding='utf-8'` reads and writes the cp1251 locale: new Cyrillic text typed in the script lands as cp1251 bytes inside a UTF-8 file, and the Write/Read tools then reject the file as non-UTF-8. Pass `encoding='utf-8'` both ways, or use Edit for any hunk with Cyrillic.
+
 For a long multi-hunk patch, write the Python script to `.asd/tmp/*.py` with the Write tool and run it (`assert old in s` per hunk); the same heredoc failure hit a patch with `"""` strings, and a docstring-quote trick (`\"` before a closing `"""`) is fragile.
+
+In some sessions `python3` in the Bash tool is a stub: it prints only "Python" and edits nothing, so a heredoc patch silently no-ops. Check `git diff --stat` after any scripted edit; `node -e` with `fs.readFileSync/writeFileSync(..., "utf8")` handles Cyrillic and keeps EOLs as they are.
